# Project Rules: GST Saathi

These rules apply across the entire codebase at all times.

## 1. Feature Development
- Build one feature at a time.
- Make small, logical commits with clear messages.
- Do not mix refactoring, documentation, and multiple features into a single change.

## 2. Agent Collaboration & Lane Ownership
- Use maximum parallel subagents with strictly owned files.
- No two lanes touch the same file.
- Edit only the files explicitly assigned to your lane.

## 3. UI & Design System
- **Plain-English UI**: Tailored for non-technical users. Use short sentences, large legible text, uncluttered layouts, and exactly one clear primary action per section.
- **Light Theme Only**: No dark mode, no pastels, no gradients, no emojis.
- **Design Tokens Only**: Use theme tokens exclusively (`background`, `surface`, `ink`, `muted`, `line`, `accent`, `accent-hover`, `on-accent`).
- **Zero Hardcoded Hex Codes**: Never hardcode hex colors in components or styles.
- **Mobile-First Responsive Design**: Design and verify for breakpoints at 375px (mobile), 768px (tablet), and 1280px (desktop).

## 4. Computation & Data Integrity
- **Tax Math**: Tax calculations must strictly be deterministic code (never LLM-generated output).
- **Data Logic**: No realistic-looking hardcoded data in application logic or business rules. Use explicit fixtures or dynamic inputs.
